<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73957" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμφᾰλό-εις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>having a navel</i> or <i>boss,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπίδοσ-οέσσης</span> of the shield
				<i>with a central boss,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.118
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Tyrt.
				12.25
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1274
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζυγὸν-όεν</span> yoke <i>with
				a knob on the top,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.269
			</span></i>, cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμφαλός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.2
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰμωγὰσ-οέσσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					1278
				</span></i>
			 (by comic transference from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπίδας
				ὀ.</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				1274
			</span></i>) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συκέης πόσιν -όεσσαν,</span>
			prob. referring to a peculiar kind of fig (called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμφάλειος</span></b>  by <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				348
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρκτον-όεσσαν,</span> because
				<i>pointing to the pole</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμφαλός</span>) of the heavens, ib.<i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>.</div>
